  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARM: Promoting of accountability and public oversight of Public Procurement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will strengthen CSOs role in procurement monitoring and help the GoA improve the Armenian public procurement system.  

It should be noted that due to the joint efforts of the Union of Informed Citizens NGO and the RA Ministry of Finance, the possibilities to oversee the handover and acceptance of procurement were significantly simplified for civil society and media. During the session of the Government on May 23 2024, the issue of making amendments and addenda to N526-N Decision of the RA Government of May 4 2017 was discussed and adopted. According to the amendments, procurement oversight opportunities are significantly simplified for civil society and media representatives, and now they have the opportunity to oversee the procurement acceptance process through simplified mechanisms and to supervise the construction process of schools, kindergartens and hospitals etc. 

The policy changes that the organization was able to achieve due to the previous project will yield the potential results. The project will increase public oversight improve accountability and develop the capacity of CSOs and media by providing relevant knowledge and skills that will create cooperation between the GoA and CSOs and media in the future.</narrative>
  </description>
